H1300.definition:
from H1299 (בָּרַק);
lightning; by analogy, a gleam; concretely, a flashing sword
KJV: bright, glitter(-ing sword), lightning.

H1301.definition:
the same as H1300 (בָּרָק);
Barak, an Israelite
KJV: Barak.

H1302.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Barkos, one of the Nethimim
KJV: Barkos.

H1303.definition:
from H1300 (בָּרָק);
a thorn (perhaps as burning brightly)
KJV: brier.

H1304.definition:
or בָּרְקַתxlit bârᵉkath corrected to bârᵉqath; from H1300 (בָּרָק);
a gem (as flashing), perhaps the emerald
KJV: carbuncle.

H1305.definition:
a primitive root;
to clarify (i.e. brighten), examine, select
KJV: make bright, choice, chosen, cleanse (be clean), clearly, polished, (shew self) pure(-ify), purge (out).

H1306.definition:
probably from H7562 (רֶשַׁע) with a prepositional prefix; with wickedness;
Birsha, a king of Gomorrah
KJV: Birsha.

H1307.definition:
patrial from H1268 (בֵּרוֹתָה);
a Berothite, or inhabitant of Berothai
KJV: Berothite.

H1308.definition:
from H1319 (בָּשַׂר); cheerful;
Besor, a stream of Palestine
KJV: Besor.

H1309.definition:
or (shortened) בְּשֹׂרָה; feminine from H1319 (בָּשַׂר);
glad tidings; by implication, reward forgood news
KJV: reward for tidings.

H1310.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to boil up; hence, to be done in cooking; figuratively to ripen
KJV: bake, boil, bring forth, roast, seethe, sod (be sodden).

H1311.definition:
from H1310 (בָּשַׁל);
boiled
KJV: [idiom] at all, sodden.

H1312.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Bishlam, a Persian
KJV: Bishlam.

H1313.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be fragrant; (compare H5561 (סַם))
the balsam plant
KJV: spice.

H1314.definition:
or בֹּשֶׂם; from the same as H1313 (בָּשָׂם);
fragrance; by implication, spicery; also the balsam plant
KJV: smell, spice, sweet (odour).

H1315.definition:
feminine of H1314 (בֶּשֶׂם) (the second form); fragrance;
Bosmath, the name of a wife of Esau, and of a daughter of Solomon
KJV: Bashemath, Basmath.

H1316.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Bashan (often with the article), a region East of the Jordan
KJV: Bashan.

H1317.definition:
feminine from H954 (בּוּשׁ);
shamefulness
KJV: shame.

H1318.definition:
a primitive root;
to trample down
KJV: tread.

H1319.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be fresh, i.e. full (rosy, (figuratively) cheerful); to announce (glad news)
KJV: messenger, preach, publish, shew forth, (bear, bring, carry, preach, good, tell good) tidings.

H1320.definition:
from H1319 (בָּשַׂר);
flesh (from its freshness); by extension, body, person; also (by euphemistically) the pudenda of aman
KJV: body, (fat, lean) flesh(-ed), kin, (man-) kind, [phrase] nakedness, self, skin.

H1321.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1320 (בָּשָׂר)
{flesh (from its freshness); by extension, body, person; also (by euphemistically) the pudenda of aman}
KJV: flesh.

H1322.definition:
from H954 (בּוּשׁ);
shame (the feeling and the condition, as well as its cause); by implication (specifically) an idol
KJV: ashamed, confusion, [phrase] greatly, (put to) shame(-ful thing).

H1323.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה) (as feminine of H1121 (בֵּן));
a daughter (used in the same wide sense as other terms of relationship, literally and figuratively)
KJV: apple (of the eye), branch, company, daughter, [idiom] first, [idiom] old, [phrase] owl, town, village.

H1324.definition:
probably from the same as H1327 (בַּתָּה);
a bath or Hebrew measure (as a means of division) of liquids
KJV: bath.

H1325.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1324 (בַּת)
{a bath or Hebrew measure (as a means of division) of liquids}
KJV: bath.

H1326.definition:
probably an orthographical variation for H1327 (בַּתָּה);
desolation
KJV: waste.

H1327.definition:
feminine from an unused root (meaning to break in pieces);
desolation
KJV: desolate.

H1328.definition:
apparently from the same as H1326 (בָּתָה) and H410 (אֵל); destroyed of God;
Bethuel, the name of a nephew of Abraham, and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Bethuel. Compare H1329 (בְּתוּל).

H1329.definition:
for H1328 (בְּתוּאֵל);
Bethul (i.e. Bethuel), a place in Palestine
KJV: Bethuel.

H1330.definition:
feminine passive participle of an unused root meaning to separate;
a virgin (from her privacy); sometimes (by continuation) a bride; also (figuratively) a city or state
KJV: maid, virgin.

H1331.definition:
masculine plural of the same as H1330 (בְּתוּלָה);
(collectively and abstractly) virginity; by implication and concretely, the tokens of it
KJV: [idiom] maid, virginity.

H1332.definition:
from H1323 (בַּת) and H3050 (יָהּ); daughter (i.e. worshipper) of Jah;
Bithjah, an Egyptian woman
KJV: Bithiah.

H1333.definition:
a primitive root;
to cut in pieces
KJV: thrust through.

H1335.definition:
from H1334 (בָּתַר);
a section
KJV: part, piece.

H1336.definition:
the same as H1335 (בֶּתֶר);
Bether, a (craggy) place in Palestine
KJV: Bether.

H1337.definition:
from H1323 (בַּת) and a masculine plural from H7227 (רַב);
the daughter (i.e. city) of Rabbah
KJV: Bath-rabbim.

H1338.definition:
from H1334 (בָּתַר); (with the article) the craggy spot;
Bithron, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Bithron.

H1339.definition:
from H1323 (בַּת) and H7651 (שֶׁבַע) (in the sense of H7650 (שָׁבַע)); daughter of an oath;
Bath-Sheba, the mother of Solomon
KJV: Bath-sheba.

H1340.definition:
from H1323 (בַּת) and H7771 (שׁוֹעַ); daughter of wealth;  the same as H1339 (בַּת־שֶׁבַע)
Bath-shua,
KJV: Bath-shua.

H1342.definition:
a primitive root;
to mount up; hence, in general, to rise, (figuratively) be majestic
KJV: gloriously, grow up, increase, be risen, triumph.

H1343.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה);
lofty; figuratively, arrogant
KJV: proud.

H1344.definition:
feminine from H1342 (גָּאָה);
arrogance
KJV: pride.

H1345.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה) and H410 (אֵל); majesty of God;
Geuel, an Israelite
KJV: Geuel.

H1346.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה);
arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament
KJV: excellency, haughtiness, highness, pride, proudly, swelling.

H1347.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה); the same as H1346 (גַּאֲוָה)xlit gaʻăvâh corrected to gaʼăvâh
{arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament}
KJV: arrogancy, excellency(-lent), majesty, pomp, pride, proud, swelling.

H1348.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה); the same as H1346 (גַּאֲוָה)xlit gaʻăvâh corrected to gaʼăvâh
{arrogance or majesty; by implication, (concretely) ornament}
KJV: excellent things, lifting up, majesty, pride, proudly, raging.

H1351.definition:
a primitive root, (rather identified with H1350 (גָּאַל), through the idea of freeing, i.e. repudiating);
to soil or (figuratively) desecrate
KJV: defile, pollute, stain.

H1353.definition:
feminine passive participle of H1350 (גָּאַל);
redemption (including the right and the object); by implication, relationship
KJV: kindred, redeem, redemption, right.

H1354.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hollow or curve; (compare H1460 (גֵּו) and H1479 (גּוּף))
the back (as rounded); by analogy, the top or rim, a boss, a vault, arch of eye, bulwarks, etc.
KJV: back, body, boss, eminent (higher) place, (eye) brows, nave, ring.

H1355.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1354 (גַב)
{the back (as rounded); by analogy, the top or rim, a boss, a vault, arch of eye, bulwarks, etc.}
KJV: back.

H1356.definition:
from H1461 (גּוּב);
a log (as cut out); also well or cistern (as dug)
KJV: beam, ditch, pit.

H1357.definition:
probably from H1461 (גּוּב) (compare H1462 (גּוֹב));
a locust (from its cutting)
KJV: locust.

H1358.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H1461 (גּוּב);
a pit (for wild animals) (as cut out)
KJV: den.

H1359.definition:
or (fully) גּוֹב; from H1461 (גּוּב); pit;
Gob, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gob.

H1360.definition:
from an unused root meaning probably to collect;
a reservoir; by analogy, a marsh
KJV: marish, pit.

H1361.definition:
a primitive root;
to soar, i.e. be lofty; figuratively, to be haughty
KJV: exalt, be haughty, be (make) high(-er), lift up, mount up, be proud, raise up great height, upward.

H1362.definition:
from H1361 (גָּבַהּ);
lofty (literally or figuratively)
KJV: high, proud.

H1363.definition:
from H1361 (גָּבַהּ);
elation, grandeur, arrogance
KJV: excellency, haughty, height, high, loftiness, pride.

H1364.definition:
or גָּבוֹהַּ; (fully) from H1361 (גָּבַהּ);
elevated (or elated), powerful, arrogant
KJV: haughty, height, high(-er), lofty, proud, [idiom] exceeding proudly.

H1365.definition:
from H1361 (גָּבַהּ);
pride
KJV: loftiness, lofty.

H1366.definition:
or גְּבֻל; (shortened) from H1379 (גָּבַל);
properly, a cord (as twisted), i.e. (by implication) a boundary; by extension the territory inclosed
KJV: border, bound, coast, [idiom] great, landmark, limit, quarter, space.

H1367.definition:
or גְּבֻלָה; (shortened) feminine of H1366 (גְּבוּל);
a boundary, region
KJV: border, bound, coast, landmark. place.

H1368.definition:
or גִּבֹּר; (shortened) intensive from the same as H1397 (גֶּבֶר);
powerful; by implication, warrior, tyrant
KJV: champion, chief, [idiom] excel, giant, man, mighty (man, one), strong (man), valiant man.

H1369.definition:
feminine passive participle from the same as H1368 (גִּבּוֹר);
force (literally or figuratively); by implication, valor, victory
KJV: force, mastery, might, mighty (act, power), power, strength.

H1370.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1369 (גְּבוּרָה);
power
KJV: might.

H1371.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be high (in the forehead);
bald in the forehead
KJV: forehead bald.

H1372.definition:
from the same as H1371 (גִּבֵּחַ);
baldness in the forehead; by analogy, a bare spot on the right side of cloth
KJV: bald forehead, [idiom] without.

H1374.definition:
plural of H1356 (גֵּב); cisterns;
Gebim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gebim.

H1375.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to be convex);
a goblet; by analogy, the calyx of aflower
KJV: house, cup, pot.

H1376.definition:
from H1396 (גָּבַר);
a master
KJV: lord.

H1377.definition:
feminine of H1376 (גְּבִיר);
a mistress
KJV: queen.

H1378.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to freeze);
crystal (from its resemblance to ice)
KJV: pearl.

H1380.definition:
from H1379 (גָּבַל) (in the sense of a chain of hills); a mountain;
Gebal, a place in Phoenicia
KJV: Gebal.

H1381.definition:
the same as H1380 (גְּבַל);
Gebal, a region in Idumaea
KJV: Gebal.

H1382.definition:
; patrial from H1380 (גְּבַל);
a Gebalite, or inhabitant of Gebal
KJV: Giblites, stone-squarer.

H1383.definition:
from H1379 (גָּבַל);
a twisted chain or lace
KJV: end.

H1384.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be arched or contracted;
hunch-backed
KJV: crookbackt.

H1385.definition:
feminine from the same as H1384 (גִּבֵּן);
curdled milk
KJV: cheese.

H1386.definition:
from the same as H1384 (גִּבֵּן);
a hump or peak of hills
KJV: high.

H1387.definition:
from the same as H1375 (גְּבִיעַ), a hillock;
Geba, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gaba, Geba, Gibeah.

H1388.definition:
by permutation for H1389 (גִּבְעָה); a hill;
Giba, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gibeah.

H1389.definition:
feminine from the same as H1387 (גֶּבַע);
a hillock
KJV: hill, little hill.

H1390.definition:
the same as H1389 (גִּבְעָה);
Gibah; the name of three places in Palestine
KJV: Gibeah, the hill.

H1391.definition:
from the same as H1387 (גֶּבַע); hilly;
Gibon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gibeon.

H1392.definition:
prolonged from H1375 (גְּבִיעַ);
the calyx of a flower
KJV: bolled.

H1393.definition:
patrial from H1391 (גִּבְעוֹן);
a Gibonite, or inhabitant of Gibon
KJV: Gibeonite.

H1394.definition:
from the same as H1375 (גְּבִיעַ); hilliness;
Gibath
KJV: Gibeath.

H1395.definition:
patrial from H1390 (גִּבְעָה);
a Gibathite, or inhabitant of Gibath
KJV: Gibeathite.

H1396.definition:
a primitive root;
to be strong; by implication, to prevail, act insolently
KJV: exceed, confirm, be great, be mighty, prevail, put to more (strength), strengthen, be stronger, be valiant.

H1397.definition:
from H1396 (גָּבַר);
properly, a valiant man or warrior; generally, a person simply
KJV: every one, man, [idiom] mighty.

H1398.definition:
the same as H1397 (גֶּבֶר);
Geber, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Geber.

H1399.definition:
from H1396 (גָּבַר); the same as H1397 (גֶּבֶר);
a person
KJV: man.
